Z||000000||Fformula88||11-18-2000||08:30 PM||||One of my g/f's classmates just bought a 91 MR2.  Before this car, he had been driving an 89 Probe.  Its a nice lookin MR2, White and in good shape.  But now he tells me my car sucks 'cause its "boxy" <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  I was more surprised than insulted.  This is the only person I ever heard call a Fiero boxy.  But its ok... 'cause my Formula will kick his 4 cyl ATX's but every time!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I think the Fiero's styling has worn VERY well.  I think my daily driver (97 Probe) looks more dated in styling than my Fiero.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||8
Z||000001||2xsess||11-18-2000||08:43 PM||||BOXY??? There isn't a square angle on the whole dang car! I agree that the Fiero styling has always seemed like it was ahead of it's time as far as the body style. <P>Jeff||||reg||1
