Z||000008||StuGood||11-19-2000||03:00 PM||||Baseless analysis (a.k.a. WAG):  g/f's classmate says your Fiero sucks because he wishes he had two things: 1) Your Fiero 2) Your g/f !  And who can blame him, right?   <P>Reminds me of a (true) fish story:<BR>   <BR>A friend called me from the airport one night, needing a ride from there to his home.  I said "sure, glad to," and took my 1986 Fiero SE to pick him up.  I figured he'd have maybe a suitcase plus a carry-on, since he was returning from a business trip to Seattle, by himself.<P>He did have those items- plus, this moving container (a 2-foot <B>cube</B>)!  Good grief.  Tied it onto the luggage rack with some string we found ("Hey -! What're you  twine to do?"   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">).    <P>Got to his house, and it turns out he'd brought back a whole mess of smoked salmon!  For my trouble, he let me have some to take home with me!  Good stuff, too   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">!  <P>Anyway - that was the only time my Fiero looked boxy to me- when it had a <B>box</B> tied onto it   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 11-19-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000009||Tryxalon||11-19-2000||05:13 PM||||Why do you care what some MR2 Driver cares about your Fiero? <P>After all, he has proven that he has no taste or standards!!!  ||||reg||1
