Z||000011||DaRkLoRD||11-19-2000||06:42 PM||||I used to read Calvin & Hobbes all the time, and I have most of the books.. I wonder if Bill Watterson licensed the Calvin image, or if someone just stole it... if he did license it to whoever makes these decals.. then I think it was slightly distasteful. (to use a comic character for this..) if not, then.. well. I still think it's bad. heh..<P>would anyone here be offended if they saw a car with the same decal, but with "Fiero" as in place of MR2? just a thought.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Standard||11-19-2000||06:59 PM||||Bill Watterson didn't license any Calvin and Hobbes images to anybody, that's why you don't see any Calvin and Hobbes shirts or cups or anything.  But I <B>really</B> want a shirt that has the picture of Calvin and Hobbes in the wagon.. Calvin is my idol   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 153,000 miles and some busted up ground f/x   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redface.gif">  <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 11-19-2000).]||||reg||1
